What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/...mmc/recovery_status
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        X20 port maintainers
Description:
                MT6797 SD per-card persistent-CRC recovery counters. Reports
                consecutive retune entries, completed degradation attempts,
                original/current UHS capability masks and reset-in-progress.
                Four consecutive retunes without a successful normal data
                request remove the current and higher UHS modes and request
                the standard MMC core card reset. A genuinely new insertion
                restores the host's original capabilities. eMMC does not use
                this SD mode degradation policy.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/...mmc/fault_crc_requests
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        X20 port maintainers
Description:
                Debug interface, present only with CONFIG_FAULT_INJECTION.
                A write of 0..32 sets a finite number of successful SD normal
                read/write completions to report -EILSEQ with zero transferred
                bytes. Does not modify DMA contents, fault tuning commands, or
                affect eMMC requests. New-card initialization clears the budget.
                Reads return the remaining budget. Intended for an unmounted
                card under an independent RAM root; default is zero. This is
                status fault injection, not an electrical CRC fault generator.
